# LiveKit voice (frontend)

Read `docs/architecture.md` (Web voice, Architectural decisions) first.

Worker-side STT/TTS and barge-in: agent API repo `docs/architecture.md` (LiveKit section) if in workspace — see `.cursorrules`.

## Room naming (`lib/livekit/room.ts`)

- Base prefix: `web-`
- **Each voice connect:** `web-{sessionId}--{connectionId}` via `livekitVoiceRoomName()`
- Pass `participantMetadata: sessionId` to `useSession` so token route resolves the chat thread
- **Do not** reuse the same room name after disconnect — LiveKit will not re-dispatch the agent

## Session lifecycle (`chat-panel.tsx`)

- `useSession` lives for the `sessionId` lifetime (not mounted only when voice is on)
- On voice enable: new `voiceConnectionId` (`crypto.randomUUID()`), then effect runs `start({ tracks: { microphone: { enabled: false } } })`
- After `start()`: `await session.room.startAudio()` for browser autoplay unlock
- PTT state in `use-voice-ptt.ts`: idle → speaking (mic ON) → thinking → answering → idle (mic OFF)
- Exit voice via keyboard button (idle/loading/error) or error primary X — not the mic button
- On voice disable / cleanup: `endVoiceSession()` → `voice_mode_exit` on `voice_control`, reset PTT state, brief settle, then `end()`
- **Do not** mount/unmount `useSession` on the voice toggle

## Push-to-talk controls (`chat-control-bar.tsx`)

| UI state | Primary button | Keyboard exit |
|----------|----------------|---------------|
| loading | Spinner, disabled | Enabled |
| idle | Mic, muted bg | Enabled |
| speaking | Mic, primary — commit turn | Disabled |
| thinking | Lightbulb, disabled | Disabled |
| answering | Red square — `stop_speech` | Disabled |
| error | White X — exit voice | Enabled |

FE timeouts (`voice-ptt-constants.ts`): 15 s idle without STT growth, 60 s max speaking, 30 s thinking → `stop_speech` + toast.

## Transcript sync (`voice-chat-sync.ts`)

Data topic: `chat_sync`

| Payload type | UI action |
|--------------|-----------|
| `voice_user` | `addVoiceMessage({ id: turnId, role: user, … })` — optional `interrupted: true` when length-truncated |
| `voice_assistant` | `addVoiceMessage({ id: turnId-assistant, role: assistant, … })` |

This is the **source of truth** for voice rows in the chat list. Interim `lk.transcription` (via `useTranscriptions` / `use-voice-turn-char-usage.ts`) drives the voice turn progress meter only — not persisted history.

## Voice turn progress (`voice-turn-progress.tsx`)

- Visible only while **speaking** (PTT), above mic + user radial chrome
- Live fill from interim STT vs `CHAT_MESSAGE_MAX` (1000); turquoise theme below 70%, amber ≥70%, red ≥90%
- 60 s countdown left of bar (synced with `VOICE_TURN_MAX_MS`)
- Meter **accumulates all STT segments** in the open turn. Reset **only** after `voice_user` `chat_sync`
- At 100%: mute mic + `voice_control` `{ "type": "user_turn_length_exceeded" }` once; UI returns to idle (mic stays OFF)

## `voice_control` (`voice-control.ts`)

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| `commit_user_turn` | PTT send with speech |
| `user_turn_length_exceeded` | Meter at 100% |
| `stop_speech` | Answering button or thinking timeout |
| `voice_mode_exit` | Leave voice session |

## Agents UI wrappers

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `agent-session-provider.tsx` | `SessionProvider` + `RoomAudioRenderer` |
| `start-audio-button.tsx` | LiveKit `StartAudio` fallback |
| `agent-wave-visualizer.tsx` | Agent wave when agent is responding |

Render `AgentSessionProvider` only while `voiceEnabled` (children need session context).

## Token route (`api/livekit/token`)

- `sessionId` from `participantMetadata` before parsing room name suffix
- `RoomConfiguration` metadata + agent dispatch on every mint
- Forward `agentMetadata.voice_language` (`en|pl|de|es|fr`) into `RoomAgentDispatch.metadata` (see `lib/livekit/voice-languages.ts`)

## Do not

- Duplicate `PersonalAgent` or scheduling logic in the frontend
- Populate chat history from room transcriptions or partial STT events
- Skip new `voiceConnectionId` on voice re-enable
- Rely on STT endpointing to end user turns (worker uses `turn_detection=manual`)
